[
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "% DOCUMENT314: grouped attained-cutoff extension; exact-new-PDF assessment pending."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "at the attained tail budget $1+C_s(1-K)K^{s-1}<2$,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "with density floor exactly at least $K$, where"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "the code family's marginal matching. The critical-tail section gives a sufficient"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Section~\\ref{sec:attained-cutoff} attains the constructive budget"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "and allows the floor to equal the cutoff."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$Q=P_{\\sqrt\\rho}$ and $T_r=M_{\\sqrt r}P_\\rho M_{\\sqrt r}$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "We also use $\\gap(r):=\\gap(T_r)$ when the density shorthand is convenient."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Here"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Theorem~\\ref{thm:attained-cutoff} below attains this constructive"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "budget with floor $b=K$; the intervening universal interval remains"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "unclassified. For $K<b<1$ the event contains every point"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\section{Attaining the constructive cutoff budget}\\label{sec:attained-cutoff}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The preceding fixed-background argument uses strict slack in both the"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "floor and the tail budget. We now remove both restrictions. The cutoff"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "event remains strictly $r>K$; mass exactly at $K$ is essential."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{theorem}\\label{thm:attained-cutoff}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Fix $0<\\rho<1$, $s=(1+\\rho)/(1-\\rho)$, and"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " k_s=\\frac{s-1}{s}<K<1,\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " g(K)=\\frac{s^s}{(s-1)^{s-1}}(1-K)K^{s-1}."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "For every integer $L\\ge1$ there is a strictly positive density $r_L$"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "on the uniform Boolean cube such that"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\mathbb Er_L=1,\\qquad r_L\\ge K,\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\mathbb E[r_L^s\\mathbf1_{r_L>K}]\\le1+g(K),"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "and $\\lambda_1(T_{r_L})\\to1$, $\\lambda_2(T_{r_L})\\to1$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Consequently $\\gap(T_{r_L})\\to0$. The same family meets every"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "prescribed floor $0<b\\le K$ and every budget $\\tau\\ge1+g(K)$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "This is an attained constructive upper budget, not a claim that"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$1+g(K)$ is the optimal threshold over all collapsing families."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{theorem}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{proof}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "All expectations below use normalized uniform probability. Write"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$Q_d=P_{\\sqrt\\rho,d}$. For positive $r$, the full spectra of"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$T_r=M_{\\sqrt r}P_{\\rho,d}M_{\\sqrt r}$ and $S_r=Q_dM_rQ_d$"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "agree, by the $AA^*/A^*A$ identity with $A=M_{\\sqrt r}Q_d$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\emph{The inherited balanced tilt.}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Use the explicit family in the proof of"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Theorem~\\ref{thm:critical-exact}. Fix a sufficiently small $d>0$ and set"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\delta_n=dn^{-1/3},\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " N(\\delta)=\\left(\\frac{(1+\\delta)^s+(1-\\delta)^s}{2}\\right)^{1/s},"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " R_n(y)=\\prod_{i=1}^n\\left(\\frac{1+\\delta_n y_i}{N(\\delta_n)}\\right)."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "In particular, the normalization is applied to every product factor."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Define"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " H_n=Q_nM_{R_n}Q_n,\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\kappa(\\delta)=\\frac{1+\\rho+"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\sqrt{(1-\\rho)^2+4\\rho\\delta^2}}{2N(\\delta)},\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " b_n=\\kappa(\\delta_n)^{-n},\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " F_n=P_{\\rho,n}+b_nH_n."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The earlier proof gives"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:attained-inherited}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " b_n\\to1,\\quad \\|H_n\\|=\\kappa(\\delta_n)^n\\to1,\\quad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\lambda_1(F_n)\\to1,\\quad\\lambda_2(F_n)\\to1,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\quad\\mathbb ER_n^s=1."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{equation}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "These are conclusions for that explicit family, not additional hypotheses."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "For completeness, its interior moments have the exact expression"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " a_n(t):=\\mathbb ER_n^t"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " =\\left(\\frac{(1+\\delta_n)^t+(1-\\delta_n)^t}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " {2N(\\delta_n)^t}\\right)^n\\longrightarrow0\\qquad(0<t<s)."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Indeed their logarithm is"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$n[t(t-s)\\delta_n^2/2+O(\\delta_n^4)]$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "At the critical exponent, $\\log\\kappa(\\delta)=O(\\delta^4)$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The block Gram comparison proved earlier has two diagonal top"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "eigenvalues one and an off-diagonal norm tending to zero; it controls"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "the actual two leading eigenvalues of $F_n$. Its second lower bound"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "is eventually positive, so it is not an added zero of the Gram matrix."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\emph{Growing finite background laws.}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The scalar optimizer from Proposition~\\ref{prop:background-optimum} has"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " v_*=\\frac{sK}{s-1}>1,\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " p_*=\\frac{(s-1)(1-K)}K\\in(0,1),\\qquad p_*v_*^s=g(K)."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "For sufficiently large $L$ choose"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " k=\\lfloor L^{1/3}\\rfloor,\\quad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " M=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{L}{2k}\\right\\rfloor,\\quad n=L-kM,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\qquad p=p_L=\\frac{\\lfloor2^kp_*\\rfloor}{2^k},"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\qquad v=v_L=K+\\frac{1-K}{p}."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Then $p\\in[p_*/2,p_*]$, $p\\to p_*$, $v\\to v_*$ and"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$v\\le V:=2v_*$. Also $k,M,n\\to\\infty$, $n\\ge L/2$ and"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$M/k\\to\\infty$. Choose exactly $2^kp$ patterns in $\\{-1,1\\}^k$,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "and let $f_L$ take value $v$ there and $K$ elsewhere."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Replace its $k$ signs by the parities of $k$ disjoint blocks of $M$"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "bits. Call the resulting background $A_L$, with high-sector indicator"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$I_L$. Independent unbiased parities give"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\mathbb EI_L=p,\\qquad A_L=K+(v-K)I_L,\\qquad\\mathbb EA_L=1."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "For a nonempty Walsh support $U$,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " Q_dM_{\\chi_U}Q_d\\chi_S"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " =\\rho^{|U|/2+|S\\setminus U|}\\chi_{S\\mathbin\\triangle U}."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Thus this weighted permutation has norm exactly $\\rho^{|U|/2}$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Each Walsh coefficient of $f_L$ has absolute value at most"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$\\mathbb E f_L=1$, and there are at most $2^k-1$ nonconstant ones."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Every substituted support has size at least $M$, so"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:attained-parity}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\|Q_{kM}M_{A_L}Q_{kM}-P_{\\rho,kM}\\|"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\le(2^k-1)\\rho^{M/2}\\longrightarrow0."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{equation}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The limit follows from $k\\log2+(M/2)\\log\\rho\\to-\\infty$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "In particular, the growing number of coefficients is explicitly"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "controlled. The scalar affine minorant gives"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:attained-dyadic-excess}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " d_L:=p_Lv_L^s-g(K)\\ge0,\\qquad d_L\\to0."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{equation}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "No uniform finite cube is assumed to realize a non-dyadic $p_*$ exactly."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\emph{Clipping, exact mean, and the amplitude reserve.}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Put $\\theta=\\min(1,s/2)$, so both $\\theta$ and $s-\\theta$ lie in $(0,s)$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "For $n=n_L$ define"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " c_n=a_n(\\theta)^{1/(2\\theta)},\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " U_n=(R_n-c_n)_+,\\qquad m'_n=\\mathbb EU_n."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Then $c_n\\to0$, $m'_n\\le a_n(1)\\to0$, and"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:attained-clipping}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\mathbb P(U_n>0)\\le\\sqrt{a_n(\\theta)},\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\|Q_nM_{U_n-R_n}Q_n\\|\\le c_n."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{equation}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The first inequality is Markov's inequality at $c_n$; the second uses"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$0\\le R_n-U_n\\le c_n$ and $\\|Q_n\\|=1$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Equality $R_n=c_n$ is in the complement of the strict event."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "For real $s>1$, $c>0$ and $z\\ge0$, the mixed-power bound is"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:attained-mixed}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " 0\\le(c+z)^s-c^s-z^s"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\le B_s\\bigl(c^{s-\\theta}z^\\theta+c^\\theta z^{s-\\theta}\\bigr),"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\qquad B_s=s2^{s-1}."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{equation}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "To see the upper bound, divide by $c^s$. For $z/c\\le1$ the"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "mean value theorem bounds the difference by $B_s(z/c)$, which is"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "at most $B_s(z/c)^\\theta$. For $z/c\\ge1$ exchange $c,z$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The lower bound follows by integrating a positive derivative."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Thus this estimate does not require an integer exponent."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Set"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{align*}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " E_L={}&K^s\\sqrt{a_n(\\theta)}\\\\"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " &+B_s\\bigl[(K^{s-\\theta}+V^{s-\\theta})a_n(\\theta)"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " +(K^\\theta+V^\\theta)a_n(s-\\theta)\\bigr],\\\\"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " e_L={}&d_L+E_L."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{align*}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Both are nonnegative and tend to zero. Eventually $e_L<1/2$ and"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$m'_n<1-K$. On that range let"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:attained-density}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\beta_L=(1-e_L)^{1/s},\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\gamma_L=\\frac{\\beta_Lm'_n}{p_L},\\qquad"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " r_L(x,y)=A_L(x)-\\gamma_L I_L(x)+\\beta_LU_n(y)."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{equation}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Here $0<\\beta_L\\le1$, $\\beta_L\\to1$ and $\\gamma_L\\to0$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The mean is exactly $1-p_L\\gamma_L+\\beta_Lm'_n=1$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The low sector has density $K+\\beta_LU_n\\ge K$; on the high sector,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " v_L-\\gamma_L=K+\\frac{1-K-\\beta_Lm'_n}{p_L}>K."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Thus mean compensation has not lowered the floor. It acts only"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "on the high sector, and no global normalization is applied."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "On the low sector the strict event is precisely $U_n>0$. Apply"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\eqref{eq:attained-mixed} with $c=K$ and $z=\\beta_LU_n$, restricted"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "to that event. Its constant contribution is at most"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$K^s\\mathbb P(U_n>0)$. The high sector is entirely above $K$;"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "discarding the nonnegative subtraction $\\gamma_L$ gives an upper"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "bound from \\eqref{eq:attained-mixed} with $c=v_L$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Averaging these bounds with probabilities $1-p_L,p_L$, the"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "coefficient of $\\beta_L^s\\mathbb EU_n^s$ is exactly one."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Use $U_n\\le R_n$, $v_L\\le V$, $\\beta_L\\le1$,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "$\\mathbb ER_n^s=1$, and \\eqref{eq:attained-clipping}. The two mixed"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "terms are bounded by those defining $E_L$. Hence"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:attained-exact-budget}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\mathbb E[r_L^s\\mathbf1_{r_L>K}]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\le p_Lv_L^s+\\beta_L^s+E_L"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " =g(K)+d_L+1-e_L+E_L=1+g(K)."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{equation}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "The reserve pays for the dyadic excess and every retained tail error."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "No convergence of $s$-moments was inferred from convergence in probability."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\emph{The actual leading eigenvalues.}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Write $P_b=P_{\\rho,kM}$, $P_t=P_{\\rho,n}$ and similarly $Q_b,Q_t$."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "By linearity and tensorization,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\["
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " S_{r_L}=(Q_bM_{A_L}Q_b-\\gamma_LQ_bM_{I_L}Q_b)\\otimes P_t"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " +\\beta_LP_b\\otimes(Q_tM_{U_n}Q_t)."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\]"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Compare with $B_L=P_b\\otimes F_n$. Since $0\\le I_L\\le1$,"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\eqref{eq:attained-parity} and \\eqref{eq:attained-clipping} imply"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\begin{align*}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " \\|S_{r_L}-B_L\\|"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": " &\\le(2^k-1)\\rho^{M/2}+\\gamma_L"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "       +\\beta_Lc_n+|\\beta_L-b_n|\\|H_n\\|\\longrightarrow0."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "\\end{align*}"
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "All four errors vanish by the established limits."
  },
  {
    "direction": "=>",
    "line": "Both tensor factors of $B_L$ are positive definite and"
  },
  {
